(6003798, 876404, 45524, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by alanfreed:</b></div><hr/><i> I gave it a 9... very nicely done!  I''m also glad to see that people are still celebrating the Festus holiday. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I thought that was Festivus? For the rest of us.  :D</td>', 'Originally posted by alanfreed: I gave it a 9... very nicely done!  I''m also glad to see that people are still celebrating the Festus holiday.   I thought that was Festivus? For the rest of us.  :D', '2010-05-12 11:46:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6003846, 878306, 93565, '<td valign="top">I think one of the most critical things missing in this photo is a sense of height or magnitude. I participate in so-called "alternative sports" and the key to a good photo is capturing the height of what''s being done. I would have voted this lower because your angle makes anything that''s going on look small and insignificant. Photography for the genre is all about building into this, and your shot goes in the opposite direction. Shoot from below, get up close- bring the action up close and personal to the viewer and blow them away with the individual''s ability to defy gravity and showcase the dynamic nature of the scene.</td>', 'I think one of the most critical things missing in this photo is a sense of height or magnitude. I participate in so-called "alternative sports" and the key to a good photo is capturing the height of what''s being done. I would have voted this lower because your angle makes anything that''s going on look small and insignificant. Photography for the genre is all about building into this, and your shot goes in the opposite direction. Shoot from below, get up close- bring the action up close and personal to the viewer and blow them away with the individual''s ability to defy gravity and showcase the dynamic nature of the scene.', '2010-05-12 12:03:05.000000', NULL, 0),
